{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"(not shown)","id":"msg_011CgzKXHe7oMAw4PVPGPud6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't edited `data/contract/sla.yaml`. AGENTS.md says agents must never edit it (\"Only the city changes it\"), and the file's own header says \"Nobody edits this file except the city. Claude Code must never change it.\" Your request goes against both, so I'd like you to confirm before I touch a contract file.\n\nThe change itself is small. In SLA-4, `wrenched_limit_hours: 48` would become `72`.\n\nThe YAML isn't the only place the 48 lives. `src/crew-queue.ts:16-19` hardcodes 48 hours for wrench deadlines instead of reading the contract, so changing the YAML alone wouldn't change the queue.\n\nHere are two ways forward:\n\n1. **The city sends the updated `sla.yaml`** (or someone authorised to make contract changes commits it). I then update `src/crew-queue.ts` to use 72 hours and add a test. This follows the repo rules.\n2. **You confirm you're authorised to make this contract change and want me to go ahead anyway.** I'll make the one-line YAML edit and update `crew-queue.ts` in the same change, so the contract and code stay in sync.\n\nWhich do you want? Either way, I can update `crew-queue.ts` now, or make it read the limit from the contract so this doesn't happen again."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":963,"cache_read_input_tokens":19660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":963},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df2f5106-8009-43fe-b803-1fc3e4848479","uuid":"f169a171-4549-4834-8292-d368323441b1","timestamp":"2026-11-13T04:46:44.351Z","request_id":"req_011CgzKXHQiNCLT1QvbhZ3Cd"}
